cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "simaudit draws on two papers listed under references: assignment consistency and order convergence follow the first (Zenodo); release comparison and observation consistency follow the second (arXiv), whose algebraic localisation method is not implemented. Please cite the papers relevant to the checks you use. Paper authorship is recorded separately from software authorship."
title: "simaudit: scoped diagnostics for simulators"
type: software
version: 0.1.0a2
date-released: 2026-11-15
repository-code: "https://github.com/TesfayZ/simaudit"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24244959
keywords:
  - reinforcement learning
  - simulator validation
  - MuJoCo
  - Gymnasium
  - numerical verification
abstract: "Scoped, reproducible diagnostics for user-supplied simulators: parameter-assignment consistency, integrator-order convergence, release comparison and observation consistency, with explicit statements of what was not assessed."
license: MIT
authors:
